"usage":{"input_tokens":38012,"output_tokens":1811,"requests":3}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"39278596a77e4ff97ea5be8351aba0060ecfed21f6296f40e980e3be5ffb8c34"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:G6","usage":{"input_tokens":246676,"output_tokens":7316,"requests":7}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Gate or caveat the p99 on sample-size adequacy: state a minimum n below which p99 is reported as 'max/insufficient-n' rather than a percentile, and require the sample size to be shown alongside each percentile so a thin-tail p99 is not presented as stable.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0975,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Step 4: 'Compute p50, p90, and p99 using an explicitly stated percentile method.'","Prior bug 1e88 telemetry table: plan-review-verifier-agentic n=6 in the 163-row window — end-to-end attested runs are plausibly single/low-double-digit","total_ms only became a durable sidecar field after task 4a40 landed, further limiting the historical end-to-end population"],"finding":"The plan mandates a p99 for each operation unconditionally, but p99 is only statistically defensible with a large sample (~100+ end-to-end observations); the attested end-to-end sidecar population may be small (the prior bug found only 6 verifier-agentic calls in its window), in which case a p99 is essentially the maximum and materially misleading.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fcd589979b87d2129","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 4 / Acceptance Criteria (p50/p90/p99 lines)","norm_id":"nd40b7c2f8bf2c339","priority":0.5025,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The end-to-end attested population for either gate is <~30 runs, so the reported p99 equals or nearly equals the max and is presented as a percentile","An agent later treats the p99 as a stable expectation and over-provisions timeouts on one-off tail runs"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an explicit exclusion for the known provider-misroute/fast-fail contaminant (per prior ticket 2876): filter on provider_provenance.ran_model, drop sub-second fast-fail/401 runs, and record the pre-fix window as excluded or separately caveated.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1812,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2876 comment on the prior bug: 'a single \"Bedrock\" gate run could be a MIX ... the misrouted arm FAILED FAST (0.2-0.4s to a 401)' and 'treat provider-attributed latency collected before change ... as unreliable'","Recommendation: 'key the A/B off provider_provenance.ran_model rather than the configured provider'","Plan step 2 lists 'workflow/provider-era filters' and 'success/failure inclusion policy' but does not name the fast-fail/misroute exclusion or the ran_model provenance key as the discriminator"],"finding":"The population-definition steps name era/success-failure/dedup filters only generically and do not call out a specific known contaminant established by prior ticket 2876: pre-fix gate runs could invisibly MIX Bedrock and direct-Anthropic traffic, with the misrouted arm failing fast (0.2–0.4s to a 401). Including such fast-failed/misrouted runs directly deflates p50 and pollutes the duration distribution.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fabab312cd41fbc1c","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan steps 2–3 (population definition / outlier handling)","norm_id":"n930b3cbc0dcebf17","priority":0.4188,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Historical rows from the pre-misrouting-fix window are included, seeding the distribution with 0.2–0.4s fast-fails that pull p50 down and corrupt the reported range","A run recorded as 'bedrock' is actually a mixed/misrouted process, so its total is not a clean single-provider wall-clock"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"In step 2's population rules, exclude runs before the provider-misrouting fix (per 2876), key provider attribution off `provider_provenance.ran_model` not the configured provider, and drop fast-fail records (e.g. sub-second 401s) with a documented threshold and count.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["4 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State a minimum sample-size threshold (e.g. n>=N) below which p90/p99 and the derived range are flagged as low-confidence, and state the default behavior when either operation falls below it.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2","F1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.265,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Step 4: 'Compute p50, p90, and p99 using an explicitly stated percentile method.'","Step 2 mentions reporting 'sensitivity or limitations where coverage differs' but sets no concrete minimum-n guard for high percentiles."],"finding":"The plan reports a p99 but does not state a minimum sample-size threshold below which the p90/p99 (and therefore the derived range) are declared statistically unreliable. With a small n, p99 is dominated by a single observation and the (p90*1.20) upper bound becomes noise.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc762be0cd7726423","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Step 4 / AC line 'Completio